"""
## Purpose and audience

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing UNIT-COMPILER behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/unit/compiler/lint/lint_still_bites_prevention_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
# @manual: primary
# REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
# @req REQ-LINT-COST-002
"""
# Lint Still Bites

**Category:** Tooling
**Status:** Implemented

## Purpose and Audience

The tempting way to make a slow linter stop timing out is to make it do less
work. Every such change -- an early return on large files, a skipped check, a
widened cache -- shows up as a faster, greener run, which looks exactly like a
successful optimisation. This spec exists so that a linter which has quietly
stopped reporting fails here instead of being congratulated.

It is aimed at anyone optimising lint cost, which is the open follow-up on the
`zca_rows.spl` budget overrun.

## Scope and Preconditions

Two committed fixtures are linted through the real `bin/simple lint`:

- a clean file, which must be reported clean;
- a file that deliberately declares a raw `rt_process_run` extern outside the
  privileged runtime tiers, which must be reported as a `RAW-RT-001` finding.

The second fixture is the load-bearing one. It is not a test of the file -- it
is a test that the linter is still looking.

## Primary Workflow

Lint each fixture and compare the reported findings against what each fixture
is known to contain. The clean file and the violating file must produce
different answers; a linter that answers "clean" to both has stopped working
regardless of how fast it did so.

## Recovery and Troubleshooting

If the violation scenario fails, do not adjust the fixture to match the new
output. Establish why `RAW-RT-001` stopped firing. A caching change that serves
a stale clean verdict for an edited file is the most likely cause, and is a
defect in the cache, not in this spec.

## Compatibility and Limitations

Covers one lint rule as a liveness canary, not lint coverage generally. It
cannot detect a linter that reports this rule while having silently dropped
others.
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.io_runtime.{process_run}

val CLEAN_FIXTURE = "test/fixtures/lint_cost/nested_expression_row.spl"
val VIOLATING_FIXTURE = "test/fixtures/lint_cost/raw_rt_violation.spl"
val DIRECT_CALL_FIXTURE = "test/fixtures/lint_cost/raw_rt_call_violation.spl"

describe "Lint still reports findings after any cost work":
    it "flags a raw runtime extern declared outside the privileged tiers":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-001 REQ-LINT-COST-002
            # @req: REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-002
            # @req: REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-003
        step("Verify: flags a raw runtime extern declared outside the privileged tiers")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Lint a fixture that declares rt_process_run directly")
        val (out, err, code) = process_run("bin/simple", ["lint", VIOLATING_FIXTURE])

        step("Require the specific rule, so a generic warning elsewhere cannot stand in for it")
        expect(out).to_contain("RAW-RT-001")
        expect(out).to_contain("rt_process_run")

        step("Require the finding to name the offending file and line, not just the rule")
        expect(out).to_contain("raw_rt_violation.spl:")

    it "does not report that finding against a file that does not contain it":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-004
        step("Verify: does not report that finding against a file that does not contain it")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Lint the clean fixture")
        val (out, err, code) = process_run("bin/simple", ["lint", CLEAN_FIXTURE])

        step("The two fixtures must produce different answers, or the linter is not reading them")
        expect(out).to_not_contain("RAW-RT-001")

        step("The clean fixture must produce no finding of its own")
        expect(out).to_not_contain("nested_expression_row.spl:")
        expect(out).to_contain("Lint passed")
        expect(code).to_equal(0)  # oracle: expected value 0 is the behavior asserted by this regression spec

    it "flags a direct call and prints actionable repair guidance":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-005
        step("Verify: flags a direct call and prints actionable repair guidance")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Lint a fixture that calls rt_process_run without declaring it")
        val (out, err, code) = process_run("bin/simple", ["lint", DIRECT_CALL_FIXTURE])
        expect(out).to_contain("RAW-RT-002")
        expect(out).to_contain("process_run")
        expect(out).to_contain("simple lint --fix")
        expect(out).to_contain("raw_rt_call_violation.spl:")
